-- W8 (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md): a default that took effect is an event
-- in the trace, with the line it was declared at and the value it gave.
--
-- It is recorded where the default is first used, so a default nothing read
-- leaves no event, and one that two rules read appears once, under the first.
-- Supplying the value with WITH takes no default, so there is nothing to record.

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN `the rate`     IS A NUMBER  TYPICALLY 3
          `has capacity` IS A BOOLEAN TYPICALLY TRUE
          `the unused`   IS A NUMBER  TYPICALLY 7
          `the venue`    IS A STRING  TYPICALLY "Singapore"

GIVETH A NUMBER
doubled MEANS `the rate` TIMES 2

GIVETH A NUMBER
tripled MEANS `the rate` TIMES 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
`both readers` MEANS doubled PLUS tripled

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`can act` MEANS `has capacity` AND TRUE

-- the default is never read: FALSE settles the AND without it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`never reads it` MEANS FALSE AND `has capacity`

GIVETH A STRING
`where it is held` MEANS `the venue`

-- two defaults, read in this order
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rate if able` MEANS IF `has capacity` THEN `the rate` ELSE 0

-- read below a function that is itself applied to an argument
GIVETH A NUMBER
`scaled by` n MEANS doubled TIMES n

-- read only when the answer is written out: nothing computes with the rate,
-- it is a field of the record returned
DECLARE Quote HAS rate IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A Quote
`quote at the rate` MEANS Quote `the rate`

#EVALTRACE doubled
#EVALTRACE doubled WITH `the rate` IS 5
#EVALTRACE `both readers`
#EVALTRACE `can act`
#EVALTRACE `never reads it`
#EVALTRACE `where it is held`
#EVALTRACE `rate if able`
#EVALTRACE `scaled by` 10
#EVALTRACE `quote at the rate`

-- a directive that is not a trace answers as before
#EVAL doubled
#ASSERT `rate if able` EQUALS 3
